Question 1: Let A = {a, b, c, d}. For each of the following partitions of A, list all the pairs of elements that form the corresponding equivalence relations:
(a) {{a, b, c}, {d}}
(b) {{a}, {b}, {c}, {d}}
(c) {{a, b, c, d}}

Question 2: Let A = {a, b, c, d}. For each of the following partitions of A, determine the elements of the corresponding equivalence relation:
(a) P1 = {{a, c}, {b, d}}
(b) P2 = {{a}, {b, c}, {d}}
(c) P3 = {{a, b}, {c, d}}
(d) P4 = {{a, b, c}, {d}}
